---
description:
  Verifies that long plain-text and markdown node/edge labels stay unwrapped on
  a single line (no automatic line breaks at spaces) when markdownAutoWrap is
  explicitly set to false, even though htmlLabels is true. Split from a single
  upstream test that rendered three config variants side by side into this
  standalone fixture.
config:
  markdownAutoWrap: false
  htmlLabels: true
title: "Testing with {\"markdownAutoWrap\":false,\"htmlLabels\":true}"
---
flowchart TD
    A["This is a really long line of plain text that will autowrap and support \n newlines too."]
    B["`This is a really long line of **markdown** text that will autowrap, unless markdownAutoWrap:false is set.`"]
    A -- "Plain text **labels** in flowcharts will autowrap,like node labels. \n Newline characters work too." --> B
    B -- "`**Markdown** edge labels will autowrap, unless markdownAutoWrap: false is set`" --> C
